From 2c0be5a6f979968736525e52f114ca9a962ef7ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhangzujian <zhangzujian.7@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 16:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Bound control I/O and status operations

Bound control client I/O with a monotonic deadline, prevent idle clients from
occupying a serial command thread for ten seconds, receive fragmented commands,
and send complete replies without blocking or raising SIGPIPE.

Run status requests through a heap-owned operation with explicit shared
lifetime. The control thread may stop waiting after four seconds while a late
scheduler callback safely completes and discards its result. Use a monotonic
condition variable so wall-clock changes cannot extend that deadline.

Also reject operations when scheduler signaling fails, initialize every queued
operation field, propagate server-side request failures through the client exit
status, and emit rate-limited stage timings for slow, timed out, or failed
control requests, including clients that never finish a command.

Signed-off-by: zhangzujian <zhangzujian.7@gmail.com>

